{"feedback": "Hypothesis: The compensatory effect (negative relationship between P/B ratio and biomass density) differs between shallow and deep strata.

Review: The implementation followed the experiment plan: densities and P/B ratio were computed at the transect level, zero‐biomass cases excluded, depth coded numerically, and a mixed‐effects model was fit with P/B_ratio ~ biomass_density * depth_code + (1|reef). The interaction term biomass_density:depth_code was non‐significant (coef ≈ 3.92×10^5, SE ≈ 4.54×10^5, p = 0.388), indicating no evidence that the slope of the P/B–biomass relationship differs by depth. Although the random‐effects variance was estimated as zero (singular covariance warnings), the fixed‐effects estimates are clear and the hypothesis was appropriately tested.

Findings: Biomass density has a strong negative effect on P/B ratio (p < 0.001), but this relationship does not differ between shallow and deep strata (interaction p = 0.388).", "success": true}
